<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sher Singh</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">assassinated 1843</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sher Singh was a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ranjit-singh">Maharaja Ranjit Singh</a> who ruled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikh-empire">Sikh Empire</a> for a short period after the deaths of his predecessors. He was assassinated in 1843 amid factional struggles at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lahore">Lahore</a> court. The Sikh Empire profile places his death in the succession of violent deaths that weakened the state before the Anglo-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikhism">Sikh</a> wars.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sher-singh.jpg" alt="Sher Singh" width="316" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ágoston Schoefft · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Painting_of_Maharaja_Sher_Singh_wearing_the_Koh-i-Noor_diamond,_by_August_Schoefft,_ca.1841%E2%80%9342.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
